WEBVTT

00:00:00.321 --> 00:00:02.608
This flask of warm broth holds about a

00:00:02.789 --> 00:00:03.912
million bacteria.

00:00:04.676 --> 00:00:07.429
Each cell grows, then splits in two, and

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:08.614
the new cells do the same.

00:00:09.277 --> 00:00:12.002
So twice the cells means twice the splitting,

00:00:12.444 --> 00:00:14.308
and the growth rate is proportional to the

00:00:14.389 --> 00:00:14.749
count.

00:00:15.491 --> 00:00:17.772
For this strain, counting in millions of cells

00:00:17.833 --> 00:00:18.332
and hours,

00:00:18.853 --> 00:00:20.954
and while the food lasts, the growth rate

00:00:21.175 --> 00:00:22.135
equals the count.

00:00:22.859 --> 00:00:25.169
A million cells gain a million an hour,

00:00:25.571 --> 00:00:27.178
and three million gain three million.

00:00:27.849 --> 00:00:28.853
Now some changes.

00:00:29.538 --> 00:00:32.644
The second flask holds a faster strain, also

00:00:32.705 --> 00:00:34.268
starting the clock with a million cells.

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:37.000
That's y equals e to the two x.

00:00:37.724 --> 00:00:40.571
The third flask holds our first strain, seeded

00:00:40.653 --> 00:00:43.220
an hour earlier, so it starts with about

00:00:43.261 --> 00:00:44.443
two point seven million.

00:00:45.046 --> 00:00:47.401
That's y equals e to the x plus

00:00:47.543 --> 00:00:47.663
one.

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:49.170
When the clock starts,

00:00:49.732 --> 00:00:51.938
which flask is gaining cells faster?

00:00:52.504 --> 00:00:52.947
Make a guess.

00:00:53.962 --> 00:00:54.529
Here's the twist.

00:00:55.153 --> 00:00:58.184
Differentiate each count, and only the fast strain

00:00:58.305 --> 00:01:00.051
gets a new factor in its derivative.

00:01:00.654 --> 00:01:02.478
By the end you'll know why, and how

00:01:02.499 --> 00:01:05.224
to differentiate k e to the a x

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:05.785
plus b.

00:01:06.422 --> 00:01:07.930
Let's graph the first flask.

00:01:08.432 --> 00:01:10.983
Time x goes along, in hours, and the

00:01:11.023 --> 00:01:13.232
count y goes up, in millions.

00:01:13.855 --> 00:01:15.842
The curve is y equals e to the

00:01:16.064 --> 00:01:16.163
x.

00:01:17.127 --> 00:01:19.230
From Year 11, the gradient at a point

00:01:19.392 --> 00:01:20.853
is the slope of the tangent,

00:01:21.536 --> 00:01:23.079
and e to the x is its own

00:01:23.119 --> 00:01:23.620
derivative.

00:01:24.202 --> 00:01:26.429
So on this graph, the gradient always equals

00:01:26.471 --> 00:01:26.851
the height.

00:01:27.675 --> 00:01:29.242
At height one, the slope is one.

00:01:29.746 --> 00:01:31.597
At about two point seven, the slope is

00:01:31.638 --> 00:01:32.644
about two point seven.

00:01:33.429 --> 00:01:35.974
Gradient divided by height is always one,

00:01:36.757 --> 00:01:37.799
and that's our measuring stick.

00:01:38.568 --> 00:01:39.911
Now the fast strain,

00:01:40.454 --> 00:01:41.557
e to the two x.

00:01:42.299 --> 00:01:46.205
Here x is doubled before the exponential acts,

00:01:46.226 --> 00:01:48.268
so the curve reaches every height in half

00:01:48.309 --> 00:01:48.669
the time.

00:01:49.532 --> 00:01:51.739
Think of it as the first curve squashed

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:52.321
sideways.

00:01:53.085 --> 00:01:55.735
This tangent triangle runs across one hour and

00:01:55.856 --> 00:01:57.462
rises about two point seven.

00:01:58.287 --> 00:02:00.904
Squash the curve, and the triangle squashes with

00:02:00.945 --> 00:02:01.005
it.

00:02:01.589 --> 00:02:03.801
The rise stays the same, but the run

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:04.645
halves.

00:02:05.389 --> 00:02:07.534
Same rise in half the run, so the

00:02:07.636 --> 00:02:08.517
slope doubles,

00:02:09.421 --> 00:02:11.806
and the whole curve squashes evenly, so that's

00:02:11.867 --> 00:02:12.869
true at every point.

00:02:13.613 --> 00:02:15.708
At height one, the slope is now two.

00:02:16.635 --> 00:02:18.402
So the derivative of e to the two

00:02:18.564 --> 00:02:20.833
x is two e to the two x.

00:02:21.617 --> 00:02:24.405
Every million cells add two million an hour.

00:02:25.128 --> 00:02:27.075
Let's put a dial on the constant a.

00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:29.905
Turn it up to three, and every run

00:02:30.007 --> 00:02:32.434
shrinks to a third, so the gradient becomes

00:02:32.616 --> 00:02:33.739
three times the height.

00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:36.388
Turn it down to a half, and every

00:02:36.409 --> 00:02:37.211
slope halves.

00:02:38.015 --> 00:02:38.859
Set it back to two,

00:02:39.362 --> 00:02:41.492
then flip the sign, to minus two.

00:02:42.296 --> 00:02:44.460
The curve mirrors over the y axis and

00:02:44.602 --> 00:02:47.127
falls, like bacteria dying in disinfectant.

00:02:47.909 --> 00:02:51.177
Every uphill tangent becomes a downhill one, just

00:02:51.219 --> 00:02:51.558
as steep.

00:02:52.222 --> 00:02:54.713
The height stays positive, because e to any

00:02:54.775 --> 00:02:55.799
power is positive.

00:02:56.524 --> 00:02:58.091
Only the slope turns negative.

00:02:58.876 --> 00:03:02.044
Whatever a is, gradient divided by height reads

00:03:02.065 --> 00:03:02.104
a.

00:03:03.068 --> 00:03:04.313
Now the early flask.

00:03:05.158 --> 00:03:07.725
Starting an hour earlier just slides the curve

00:03:07.967 --> 00:03:08.708
one hour left.

00:03:09.535 --> 00:03:11.007
Sliding doesn't tilt anything.

00:03:11.511 --> 00:03:13.934
Each tangent moves with its point and keeps

00:03:13.995 --> 00:03:14.415
its slope,

00:03:15.137 --> 00:03:16.979
so the derivative of e to the x

00:03:17.021 --> 00:03:19.103
plus one is just e to the x

00:03:19.124 --> 00:03:19.544
plus one.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:21.152
Back to your guess.

00:03:21.736 --> 00:03:24.043
When the clock starts, the early flask has

00:03:24.084 --> 00:03:26.872
about two point seven million cells, gaining about

00:03:26.913 --> 00:03:28.236
two point seven million an hour.

00:03:28.879 --> 00:03:31.427
The fast strain has one million, gaining two

00:03:31.468 --> 00:03:32.029
million an hour.

00:03:32.591 --> 00:03:35.458
So the early flask gains faster, but only

00:03:35.519 --> 00:03:36.841
because it has more cells.

00:03:37.685 --> 00:03:40.231
Per cell, the fast strain grows twice as

00:03:40.272 --> 00:03:40.592
fast.

00:03:41.195 --> 00:03:43.743
That's what a measures, the gradient compared with

00:03:43.764 --> 00:03:44.105
the height.

00:03:44.889 --> 00:03:48.086
Last change: three identical flasks, counted together.

00:03:48.509 --> 00:03:51.038
That's y equals three e to the x.

00:03:51.641 --> 00:03:54.176
Every count and every growth rate is three

00:03:54.237 --> 00:03:54.760
times bigger.

00:03:55.445 --> 00:03:57.385
On the graph, the curve stretches upward.

00:03:57.828 --> 00:03:59.515
The run stays the same, but the rise

00:03:59.596 --> 00:04:01.865
triples, so every slope triples.

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:05.096
That's the Year 11 constant multiple rule: the

00:04:05.117 --> 00:04:06.359
three comes along for the ride.

00:04:07.002 --> 00:04:08.846
But each cell grows at the same pace,

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:11.533
so gradient divided by height is still one.

00:04:12.217 --> 00:04:12.497
Only a

00:04:13.322 --> 00:04:13.904
changes that.

00:04:14.582 --> 00:04:16.675
Now let's prove it, with the Year 11

00:04:16.735 --> 00:04:17.258
chain rule.

00:04:17.862 --> 00:04:20.079
Take y equals e to the a x

00:04:20.139 --> 00:04:20.562
plus b.

00:04:21.266 --> 00:04:24.078
Call the inside part u, so u equals

00:04:24.259 --> 00:04:25.102
a x plus b.

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:28.174
Then y equals e to the u, and

00:04:28.214 --> 00:04:30.421
since that's its own derivative, d y by

00:04:30.462 --> 00:04:31.967
d u is e to the u.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:34.814
The inside part's derivative, d u by d

00:04:35.016 --> 00:04:36.960
x, is just a, because b is a

00:04:36.981 --> 00:04:37.401
constant.

00:04:38.104 --> 00:04:39.989
The chain rule multiplies them, e to the

00:04:40.171 --> 00:04:40.731
u, times a.

00:04:41.797 --> 00:04:43.625
Put the inside part back, and you get

00:04:43.907 --> 00:04:45.574
a e to the a x plus b.

00:04:46.339 --> 00:04:48.066
The b stays in the power but adds

00:04:48.146 --> 00:04:50.396
no factor, just like the early flask.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.932
And with k out the front, k just

00:04:52.993 --> 00:04:53.516
rides along.

00:04:54.263 --> 00:04:54.828
Let's use it.

00:04:55.412 --> 00:04:57.949
Differentiate y equals e to the three x.

00:04:58.734 --> 00:05:00.279
The inside part is three x,

00:05:00.781 --> 00:05:02.245
and its derivative is three.

00:05:03.048 --> 00:05:05.013
So keep e to the three x exactly

00:05:05.073 --> 00:05:06.879
as it is, and multiply by three.

00:05:07.501 --> 00:05:09.436
The derivative is three e to the three

00:05:09.577 --> 00:05:09.698
x.

00:05:10.528 --> 00:05:10.977
One trap.

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:13.190
Don't bring the power down like you would

00:05:13.231 --> 00:05:14.053
for x cubed.

00:05:14.616 --> 00:05:16.557
That rule needs x in the base, and

00:05:16.618 --> 00:05:18.879
here x is in the power, so the

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:20.180
exponential stays whole.

00:05:20.722 --> 00:05:22.058
Now all three constants.

00:05:22.702 --> 00:05:25.287
Find f prime of minus three, where f

00:05:25.307 --> 00:05:27.411
of x equals five e to the two

00:05:27.552 --> 00:05:28.453
x plus six.

00:05:29.336 --> 00:05:30.519
So k is five, a

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:32.845
is two and b is six.

00:05:33.828 --> 00:05:36.717
Copy the exponential, then multiply by k and

00:05:36.917 --> 00:05:37.038
a.

00:05:37.941 --> 00:05:40.310
Five times two is ten, so f prime

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.057
of x is ten e to the two

00:05:42.177 --> 00:05:42.920
x plus six.

00:05:43.846 --> 00:05:45.071
Now substitute minus three.

00:05:45.895 --> 00:05:48.085
Two times minus three, plus six, is zero,

00:05:48.466 --> 00:05:49.973
and e to the zero is one.

00:05:50.597 --> 00:05:52.464
So f prime of minus three is ten.

00:05:53.633 --> 00:05:54.196
Check the graph.

00:05:54.739 --> 00:05:56.787
It's five high there, with a slope of

00:05:56.867 --> 00:05:59.257
ten, twice the height, as a equals two

00:05:59.317 --> 00:05:59.658
predicts.

00:06:00.483 --> 00:06:01.409
Here's a way to hold onto it.

00:06:01.872 --> 00:06:02.999
Think of the flasks.

00:06:03.882 --> 00:06:05.664
a is the growth per cell,

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:08.287
so it sets the gradient compared with the

00:06:08.327 --> 00:06:08.567
height.

00:06:09.688 --> 00:06:11.894
b is the start time, so it slides

00:06:11.934 --> 00:06:13.799
the curve but adds no new factor.

00:06:14.621 --> 00:06:17.651
k is how many flasks, so it scales

00:06:17.711 --> 00:06:18.935
heights and slopes together.

00:06:19.716 --> 00:06:20.076
In short,

00:06:20.616 --> 00:06:23.199
copy the exponential, then multiply by k

00:06:23.779 --> 00:06:24.440
and by a.

00:06:27.221 --> 00:06:27.627
Your turn.

00:06:28.255 --> 00:06:31.221
Differentiate f of x equals four e to

00:06:31.262 --> 00:06:33.848
the two x minus one, then find f

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:35.231
prime of a half.

00:06:36.237 --> 00:06:37.348
Pause here to answer.

00:06:48.061 --> 00:06:50.391
The inside part is two x minus one,

00:06:50.853 --> 00:06:52.139
with derivative two.

00:06:52.821 --> 00:06:53.041
So f

00:06:53.723 --> 00:06:56.369
prime of x is four times two, e

00:06:56.911 --> 00:06:58.775
to the two x minus one, which is

00:06:58.936 --> 00:07:00.419
eight e to the two x minus one.

00:07:01.001 --> 00:07:03.087
At a half, the power is zero, and

00:07:03.167 --> 00:07:05.173
e to the zero is one, so f

00:07:05.214 --> 00:07:06.919
prime of a half is eight.

00:07:07.702 --> 00:07:09.913
If you got four, you dropped the factor

00:07:09.933 --> 00:07:10.958
of two from the inside.

00:07:12.814 --> 00:07:13.361
Last one.

00:07:14.048 --> 00:07:17.160
A curve has equation y equals three e

00:07:17.241 --> 00:07:18.284
to the minus two x.

00:07:19.028 --> 00:07:21.414
Find its gradient at x equals zero,

00:07:22.037 --> 00:07:24.383
and explain why the curve is decreasing for

00:07:24.564 --> 00:07:25.045
every x.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:27.021
Pause here to answer.

00:07:37.821 --> 00:07:40.327
The derivative is three times minus two, e

00:07:40.968 --> 00:07:43.334
to the minus two x, which is minus

00:07:43.394 --> 00:07:45.159
six e to the minus two x.

00:07:45.942 --> 00:07:47.837
At zero, that's minus six.

00:07:48.581 --> 00:07:50.727
E to any power is positive, so e

00:07:50.968 --> 00:07:53.134
to the minus two x is always positive.

00:07:53.816 --> 00:07:56.620
Times minus six, the gradient is negative for

00:07:56.821 --> 00:07:59.424
every x, so the curve is always decreasing.

00:08:00.208 --> 00:08:02.044
It isn't because the curve dips below zero.

00:08:02.548 --> 00:08:03.115
It never does.

00:08:04.928 --> 00:08:08.156
Next, a strain that doubles exactly every hour

00:08:08.358 --> 00:08:10.082
has a count of two to the x.

00:08:11.045 --> 00:08:13.348
Is two to the x secretly e to

00:08:13.409 --> 00:08:14.810
some number times x?

00:08:15.673 --> 00:08:17.621
Find that number, and you can differentiate it

00:08:17.663 --> 00:08:18.204
the same way.

00:08:20.828 --> 00:08:21.691
Here are the key notes.

00:08:22.094 --> 00:08:23.641
Pause the video if you need more time

00:08:23.683 --> 00:08:24.144
to copy them.
